# DraftWise — Full Feature Build Plan

**Slogan:** Every draft checked. Every change explained.

This plan covers all 12 requested areas (demo, Gmail, dashboard, chatbot, drift alerts, phishing, landing page, UI/UX, SEO/technical, classification, PDF requirements, and final fixes). The codebase is a Next.js 16 / FastAPI monorepo with Supabase auth and PostgreSQL.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Gmail OAuth** (P3) requires a Google Cloud project with the `gmail.readonly` scope and an OAuth client ID/secret. These credentials are **not** in the repo. The plan will build the full UI/backend plumbing; it will work end-to-end only once you supply `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` to the backend `.env`.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Custom domain** (item 9) — we will configure `next.config.ts` with a `SITE_URL` env var and generate all canonical/og tags from it. The DNS step is out-of-scope (requires your registrar access). We will set `SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000` for dev.

> [!WARNING]
> **AI provider** — current `.env` uses Gemini or Morpheus. The chatbot and classification improvements use the same provider via the existing adapter. No new API key is needed; classification will improve via better prompts + WSD logic rather than a trained model (which would require an annotation dataset not yet available).

> [!NOTE]
> **Image generation** — the user said "ignore the image gen if you can't do that, just make a container with image description." We will create styled placeholder containers with accessible descriptions for all image assets. Logo will be an SVG.

