### 6 — Phishing / Spam Detection

#### [NEW] `backend/app/services/email_safety.py`
- Signal extraction (no external fetching):
  - Sender/reply-to domain mismatch
  - Deceptive URLs (display host ≠ actual host)
  - Credential/payment request keywords
  - Suspicious attachment types (.exe, .js, .scr etc.)
  - Gmail spam label (if available from import)
- Output: `risk_state` = `clear|suspected_phishing|spam|insufficient_evidence`
- HTML sanitisation before any AI processing
- High-risk → safety queue; authorised reviewer releases with reason

#### [MODIFY] `backend/app/api/classify.py`
- After classification, run `email_safety.assess(email)` and store `risk_state`
- High-risk emails are gated from automatic downstream AI processing

#### [MODIFY] `frontend/app/(workspace)/inbox/page.tsx`
- Show risk badge (Spam / Suspected Phishing / Clear) on email rows
- Filter by risk state

